# Blockchain Layer Rules

## Golden Rule

**The user must never know they're using a blockchain.**

- No transaction signing prompts (Circle Modular Wallets handles this)
- No "approve spend" dialogs
- No gas fee display
- No network switching
- No wallet address shown by default

---

## Arc Testnet — Network Configuration

```typescript
// lib/arc/config.ts — single source of truth for all network constants
export const ARC_TESTNET = {
  chainId: 5042002,           // decimal; hex: 0x4CEF52
  name: 'Arc Testnet',
  rpcUrl: 'https://rpc.testnet.arc.network',
  wsUrl: 'wss://rpc.testnet.arc.network',
  explorerUrl: 'https://testnet.arcscan.app',
  faucetUrl: 'https://faucet.circle.com',
  nativeCurrency: {
    name: 'USDC',
    symbol: 'USDC',
    decimals: 18,             // USDC as native gas token uses 18 decimals
  },
} as const;

// ⚠️ USDC has DUAL decimal representation on Arc:
//   - As native gas token: 18 decimals
//   - As ERC-20 token balance/transfer: 6 decimals
// Always use 6 decimals when reading ERC-20 balances or calling token contracts.
```

