## Error Handling

```typescript
try {
  const result = await depositToUSYC({ walletClient, amountUsdc });
  return result;
} catch (error) {
  console.error('[USYC deposit failed]', { amountUsdc, error });
  // Never expose blockchain error details to user
  throw new Error('Transaction could not be completed. Please try again.');
}
```

User-facing error messages:
- Deposit failed → "Something went wrong — we'll retry in a moment"
- Entitlement error → "Your account isn't set up for this yet — contact support"
- Network slow → "Arc is taking a moment — your transaction is still on the way"
- Insufficient balance → "Your available balance is $X — we've adjusted the plan"

